<title>USA: BEFORE THE BELL - IBM slumps after EPS news.</title>
<headline>BEFORE THE BELL - IBM slumps after EPS news.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>International Business Machines Corp shares slumped preceding Monday's U.S. market open in the wake of quarterly earnings that exceeded official analyst estimates but fell short of Wall Street's &quot;whisper number,&quot; traders said.</p>
<p>Ahead of the market open, IBM slipped 1-5/8 to 127-3/4.</p>
<p>IBM said this morning it earned $2.45 per share in the third quarter versus $2.30 in the year-ago period, excluding a charge.</p>
<p>The third quarter net was $0.02 per share above the First Call analysts' consensus estimate, but traders said the most recent earnings bar set for the period was $2.53.</p>
